VIOLATION — MUST-2: when a rule targets a behaviour the agent is prone to rationalize, it MUST
include the exact excuse phrases marked BLOCKED. This rule targets exactly such a behaviour —
skipping a declaration header because the migration feels far away — and its BLOCKED section
holds six ABSTRACT CATEGORY LABELS instead of the sentences a session actually writes.

The six entries are "Cost-deferral reasoning about migration effort," "Scope-boundary appeals
concerning the current ticket," "Vendor-stability assumptions," "Reversibility
overestimation," "Documentation-substitution patterns," and "Prototype-exemption claims."
Each is a taxonomy of an error type, phrased in the third person, in the vocabulary of
someone classifying mistakes rather than making one. No session has ever written any of those
strings. A tripwire that matches nothing traps nothing, which is the whole failure mode
MUST-2's own `**Why:**` names: abstract framing is trivially rationalized, and only the
verbatim phrase blocks the rationalization at the linguistic level.

The defect is not that the corpus is missing. The heading is present, the list is present,
the entry count is the same six the compliant sibling carries. What is missing is that the
entries are literal.

Discriminator 1 — MUST-1 IS SATISFIED. Every load-bearing sentence in both numbered clauses
uses MUST or MUST NOT, and the alternatives are named BLOCKED rather than discouraged. Not
one "should," "prefer," "consider" or "try to" appears as a clause modal. A judge citing
MUST-1 has named a defect this file does not contain.

Discriminator 2 — MUST-3 IS SATISFIED. Both clauses carry a two-armed DO / DO NOT block, and
the arms differ in substance: the first shows a specific exit path against a "TBD"
placeholder and a bare import, the second shows an enqueued job against a direct vendor call
on a request path.

Discriminator 3 — MUST-4 IS SATISFIED. Both clauses and the MUST NOT section carry a
`**Why:**` line, each one sentence, each naming the failure mode rather than restating the
clause.

Discriminator 4 — MUST-5, MUST-6 and MUST-7 ARE SATISFIED. Frontmatter declares `priority: 10`
with `scope: path-scoped` and a matching `paths:` list; Origin cites
`journal/0402-INCIDENT-queue-vendor-migration.md` § 2 with the measured overrun it recorded.

Discriminator 5 — MUST-8 IS NOT ENGAGED. No CLI-divergent content appears: no delegation
syntax, no tool names, no native-primitive references.

Discriminator 6 — MUST-9 IS NOT ENGAGED (no empirical-validation fixtures ship with this rule)
and MUST-10 / MUST-11 ARE NOT ENGAGED (`priority: 10` + `scope: path-scoped`, which Rule 10's
Trigger-scope paragraph excludes).

Discriminator 7 — THE `## MUST NOT` BULLETS ARE SATISFIED. Every `**Why:**` is one sentence;
no hedging phrase appears inside a MUST clause; the Detection row names parsed import nodes
and a manifest field rather than booking a lexical detector; the file is well under 200 lines.

The whole defect is six entries written as categories where the meta-rule requires sentences.
